  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The gate consumes every depth's features, including long-context features. Selecting a shallow output therefore does not isolate recent history or demonstrate reduced stale-interest influence.",
    "Reproduction requires the baseline dilation schedule, receptive fields, projection and gate dimensions, initialization, normalization, checkpoint-selection rule, and measured runtime. Difficulty 3/10 is provisional without the supplied baseline implementation.",
    "A learned gate changes both capacity and feature aggregation. Fixed aggregation and parameter-matched controls are needed to distinguish adaptive context selection from added parameters or normalization.",
    "No baseline validation HR@10, paired uncertainty analysis, or budgeted trial schedule is supplied. Repeated selection on 200 validation users per category risks validation overfitting; retain seed 42 and the pinned evaluator.",
    "Mean cosine similarity near zero rules out strong average directional alignment, but does not establish broadly dispersed or full-rank embeddings. Training margins also do not identify stale context as the cause of Electronics errors.",
    "Originality and potential ratings are subjective. The comparison with prior multiscale convolutional gating needs closer verification; simulator feedback from twenty users supports hypotheses rather than general claims about intent."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Clarify novelty and whether the architecture actually controls historical influence while preserving NextItNet causality.",
      "query": "NextItNet sequential recommendation adaptive multiscale dilated causal convolution depth gating: which prior methods learn position-wise weights over intermediate residual blocks, how are receptive fields and padding handled, and can a gate conditioned on deepest features still depend on old interactions when selecting shallow features?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Define controls that distinguish adaptive context selection from extra capacity and make implementation cost assessable.",
      "query": "For jointly trained multiscale gated causal convolutional sequential recommenders, what ablations compare learned depth gates with fixed uniform aggregation, final-block readout, and parameter-matched projections? What initialization, normalization, gate-collapse diagnostics, parameter overhead, and GPU-memory costs are reported?"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Strengthen evaluation without changing the host benchmark or using hidden test data.",
      "query": "Sequential recommendation sampled HR@10 evaluation with 200 fixed validation users per category and 99 unique negatives: how should paired user-level bootstrap uncertainty, four-category macro averaging, and repeated validation model-selection bias be assessed while keeping training seed, candidate sets, and evaluator fixed?"
    }
  ]
}
